$DIR/test.p:3:13: cannot use 98.6 (untyped float constant) as int value in variable declaration (truncated)
    A constant with a fraction is used as an integer. Converting it would lose
    the fraction, which Plutonium, like Go, does not do silently for constants.
    Use an integer constant, or convert a variable at run time.
    (see "Representability" in the Plutonium spec, section 8.5)
    (run "pluto explain E0043" for a longer explanation)
